==================================================================================================
 (1) THE EISENSTEIN STRUCTURE OF 183 = Phi_6(14)
==================================================================================================
  Phi_6(14) = 14^2-14+1 = 183;  factor 183 = 3 * 61 (both primes = 3 mod 4 ... 3, 61=1 mod4)
  powers of 14 mod 183: [14, 13, 182, 169, 170, 1]
  signed:               [14, 13, -1, -14, -13, 1]   <- the 6 Eisenstein units {+-1,+-13,+-14}; ORDER of 14 = 6
  => 14^2 = 13 (=13), 14^3 = 182 (=182=-1), so 14*13 = 14^3 = -1 mod 183.
  ODD/EVEN: order 6 = 2 * 3 = (antipode Z/2: 14^3=-1) x (Eisenstein Z/3: 14^2=13). The '2' is the
           complement/antipode (14 even =2*7), the '3' is the Eisenstein 6th-root (3 | 183).

==================================================================================================
 (2) THE COMB RESONANCE at t* = 14/183
==================================================================================================
  ||13 t*|| = ||182/183|| = ||182/183|| = 1/183  (= 1/183: the tiny step)
    r  comb span (r-1)/183  < 1/14?
    2                1/183      YES  (0.0055 vs 0.0714)
    3                2/183      YES  (0.0109 vs 0.0714)
    5                4/183      YES  (0.0219 vs 0.0714)
